From e7f05a5a32c81eceb07587e0f572766e111d1f16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:18:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add reusable FAQPage structured data for Data Guide
 articles

Pages with a visible FAQ section can now opt into FAQPage schema.org
structured data by setting `faq: true` in frontmatter. The MDX body is
parsed once per build to lift the questions and answers out of the
'## Frequently asked questions' (or '## FAQ') section, and the SEO
component emits them as JSON-LD inside the article '@graph'.

- src/utils/extractFaq.ts: tolerant Markdown parser that handles both the
  H3-pair FAQ shape and the <details>/<summary> shape, with a plain-text
  helper that strips Markdown links and inline code so answers match the
  visible page copy word for word (what Google's FAQPage schema wants).
- src/utils/structuredData.ts: new faqStructuredDataNode helper and an
  optional faqs argument on articleStructuredData that appends FAQPage to
  the article '@graph' only when entries are present.
- gatsby-node.ts: reads the raw MDX for pages with faq: true, extracts
  the Q/A pairs, and passes them through page context. Panics on build
  if a page opts in but has no FAQ section, so the flag can't rot.
- src/components/seo.tsx, src/templates/docs.tsx,
  src/interfaces/Layout.interface.ts: thread the faqs through from page
  context to the <script type="application/ld+json"> tag.
- scripts/check-faq-jsonld.mjs: utility to print the FAQPage JSON-LD a
  page will emit, for eyeball review against the visible page text.

Tests cover the plain-text transform, both FAQ shapes, the empty-page
fallback, the article-graph append, and the real 5-ways-to-host MDX.
